     promoter        1..56
                     /label="PtetR* (pRAB)"
                     /synonym="pR* w/o tetO"
                     /synonym="tetR promoter (pRAB)"
                     /note="PtetR* (pRAB): the tetR promoter of the pRAB Tet
                     vectors, annotated in pRAB11 (JN635500) as 'pR* w/o tetO'.
                     It overlaps a modified copy of the Tn10 tet control region:
                     its 3' half is J01830 1545-1574 read on the tetR strand,
                     with two substitutions (J01830 1552 C>T and 1554 C>A on the
                     tetA strand) that turn the Tn10 sequence there into the
                     consensus -10 TATAAT; its -35, TTGACA, lies in vector
                     sequence upstream of the Tn10 homology. The same two
                     changes fall in the Tn10 operator O1 that the region
                     overlaps, which the record marks 'w/o tetO'. The -35 and
                     -10 below are predicted by the catalog's criteria
                     (tools/promoter_boxes.py), not mapped; no transcription
                     start is mapped for this promoter. On the opposite strand
                     the same bases read as the -35 and operator of a tetA-type
                     promoter with two changes, which is why partial
                     tet-promoter hits used to land here."
                     /db_xref="SO:0000167"
                     /db_xref="GenBank:JN635500"
                     /citation=[1]
